{
  "subtitle": "family/next: 1.1M env steps each, size50m, 30 fixed worlds (tools/death_eval.py). next_lam0 is masked (reads the game's action rules): counted as cheating. next_nomask is the honest run. Updated 2026-11-09.",
  "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over 30 evaluation episodes, \u00b1 its standard error over those worlds; unlock rates are the share of episodes in which an achievement fired; return is the mean raw Craftax return as a % of the maximum (226). Every checkpoint is scored on the same fixed worlds (env.reseed, audit B05), so comparisons are paired world by world. The error bars cover the worlds only, not training seeds.\nPlain DreamerV3 (abl_plain, seed 0) scores 4.77 \u00b1 0.28, level with vanilla DreamerV3 on the original code (4.63 \u00b1 0.22); normalized return 1.71% and 1.65%.\nThe next agent with the rule mask and taste on the manager at lam_mgr 0 (no taste), next_lam0, scores 11.20 \u00b1 0.41 (4.56% return) on these worlds and 11.30 \u00b1 0.27 on 60 worlds, the best run of the project. It is MASKED: the mask reads the game's action rules, so it is counted as cheating and is not a headline result. The honest run, next_nomask (the same agent with the mask off), scores 5.63 \u00b1 0.27 on these worlds and 5.82 \u00b1 0.17 on 60: level with v12_nomask (6.03; 6.13 on 60 worlds) and about one achievement above plain. Without the mask the next agent's lead over v1.2 is gone; the mask was worth about 5.5 achievements to it.",
  "table_note": "ach. \u00b1 SE = mean episode-final achievements \u00b1 standard error over the 30 worlds (one training seed, so seed variation is not included). w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. return = raw Craftax return, % of 226. Rates are % of episodes. Vanilla DreamerV3: the original checkpoint (code before the 2026-10 fixes), re-scored on the fixed worlds. Plain (new code): `--configs craftax size50m --env.craftax.survival none`; the row shows seed 0 (seed 1 also scores 4.77). Next, no taste: next_lam0, the next agent (RSSM-2 memory, curiosity, 13 named goals, shared critic, hold 32) with the rule mask and a taste that adds exactly zero (lam_mgr 0); MASKED, counted as cheating. A 30-world score moves by about \u00b10.55 between world sets: gaps under ~1.1 between single runs are not evidence.",
